  "question": "You have a 7*7 matrix with some positions already filled with numbers and others marked with 0. The matrix is:\n3 6 0 0 1 7 25\n9 7 8 0 0 0 42\n0 0 0 0 0 3 31\n2 0 8 0 0 0 25\n0 0 8 0 0 0 34\n0 0 0 0 0 0 29\n19 30 32 41 29 35 186\nThe last number in each row and column represents the sum of all other numbers in that row or column. You need to fill in the 0 positions using the numbers [1, 9, 3, 8, 4, 1, 5, 4, 1, 1, 6, 3, 1, 7, 7, 2, 7, 5, 9, 7, 7, 5, 8, 8, 5] to satisfy these conditions. Each number can only be used once.\n\nIMPORTANT: When you finish, put ONLY the final answer inside \\boxed{...} (no extra text). If the task requests a multi-line format, encode it into a single line representation.",
  "steps": [
